# Cargo Clippy

After changing Rust code (`*.rs`, `Cargo.toml`), run Clippy and clear every warning before considering the work done.

```bash
cargo clippy --all-targets
```

## Requirements

- Treat Clippy warnings as must-fix (do not leave `warn` output unresolved)
- Prefer fixing the code over `#[allow(...)]`; allow only when the warning is a false positive and note why
- Re-run Clippy after fixes until it reports no warnings
- Include lib/bin/tests: use `--all-targets` so test and example code is checked too

## Example

```text
# ❌ BAD — ship with Clippy noise
warning: struct `Locks` has a public `len` method, but no `is_empty` method

# ✅ GOOD — address the lint
impl Locks {
    pub fn len(&self) -> usize { ... }
    pub fn is_empty(&self) -> bool { self.root.packages.is_empty() }
}
```
